# Milestone: M3 (lone-sleeper wake activated at v1.0 / M10, design-risks v0.11.4-A)
# Covers: a strand calls sleep(100ms); it parks on the sleep queue.  After the
#         host advances the virtual clock past the deadline, urbi_step's
#         pre-dispatch sleep-queue pump wakes it and it resumes, running the
#         statement after the sleep (Realm.woke = 1).
# matrix-row: temporal-sleep
#
# Pre-v1.0 the lone sleeper was never woken: the sleep wake ran only inside the
# post-dispatch fix-up (urbi_sched_post_dispatch step 3), which a VM whose sole live
# strand is sleeping never reached (no dispatch -> the loop breaks before the
# wake).  v0.11.4-A added urbi_sched_wake_due_sleepers as a pre-dispatch pump in
# urbi_step (mirroring the periodic pre-pump), so a lone expired sleeper resumes.
#
# v0.13.3 (refactor-3 SCHED-01/B10): the step now reports QUIESCENT, not
# RUNNING.  The woken strand completes and dies inside this step; under the
# single-writer runnable count (WAITING strands are no longer counted, and the
# park/wake cycle no longer leaves a phantom +1 behind) nothing live remains
# afterwards.  The pre-fix RUNNING was the leaked count — a host busy-spin
# signal.
#
## host: realm sleeper
## host: run Realm.woke = 0
## host: run sleep(100ms); Realm.woke = 1
## host: run Realm.woke
## host: advance-clock 200
## host: step 5000
## host: run Realm.woke
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 1
